{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 4f801add015f09c1428839ae244b643516762f9c (tree fd195476c99453f543bd78c1b4c16668a8b94ebd), E5 sequential authorization dependencies on published main 42d35b88. The verdict binds the E5 implementation promise adf6f94b and signs all 17 path artifacts, with scope-client.ts first.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Artifacts.** The 17 filed artifacts equal the 17 changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only 42d35b88 4f801add`): none missing, none extra, none twice.\n- **Gate.** `gate.txt` (SHA-256 `926456ed…`) names head ec98e1f6 and tree 41535a1b, shows \"changed files 0\", ends \"gate passed\", and `gate.exit` reads 0 (1,275.10 s). Node 246, Counting 60, Plain 5,107 with one skipped, Native 1,240 with two skipped, crossings 0 lost, 3 stale, 0 unowned. The generated client case ran 400 seeds in 474.57 s inside its 600 s deadline. END act 97f94081 records the run.\n- **Continuation.** `git diff ec98e1f6 4f801add` changes one file, the implementation note, so the review head needs no second gate. The failed gate at b93aa01d (END c602377c) stays a separate record in the note and is not relabelled.\n- **Hashes.** All 13 distinct SHA-256 values in the note match files in the three retained evidence directories.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main (42d35b88) is clean with tree fd195476. `git diff --check` is clean. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 18 commits. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings.\n- **Named cases.** I read the code paths and the tests for cases 3, 5 and 9, invariant 11, the same-key version refusal and \"no signing before exact source resolution\". The full gate passed all of them. I did not rerun them.\n\n## Wake rate\nThe head adds no Durable Object alarm, no retry and no server request, so the wake floor and requests per room per hour do not change. It adds client-side timers only. A `submit` or `fill` that waits holds one timer at the earlier of its own deadline and the pending source's deadline. The publication pass holds one client timer at the earliest such wake. Each timer fires once. Both stop once the waiting request reaches its source or deadline, and a wake always lies in the future (`#sourcesReady` throws `source` once either deadline passes), so no loop can form. The cost is local: every `#sync` now reads the authorization records and inspects each retained source, with no network call.\n\n## Architecture\n- A dependent authorization names its sources by key and version. `#sourcesReady` rechecks every exact source at each read, and a recorded same-key earlier version returns the input for revision. `#waitForSources` subscribes before it inspects, so an event during the fence cannot be lost.\n- A hypothetical chain explores under E2's checked standing (`judgeExploreGrant`) in one cut. `current()` fails when the cut, the session, the clock or a projected timer moves. An unchecked `also.via` stops before custody.\n- The private composition path (`registerComposition`) is not exported from the package entry. Public composition stays with the later ActEnvironment, as ruling f364097e says.\n- `ClientView.requests` widens to include `AuthorizationRequestView` (`is: \"authorization\"`, status `waits` or `source`), exported from `scope.ts`. A consumer that switches on `is` must handle the new member. The note states the view.\n\n## Security\n- **No signing before the exact source records.** `#signRetained` calls `#sourcesReady` before `fill` and `permit`, and refuses `source` when a source is not ready. The custody build repeats the check under its fence and compares the signed materialization with the one the caller saw (`expected`). A deadline that passes on a dependent reports `source`.\n- **Hypothetical prefix.** It uses the held read session and E2's standing. It cannot extend standing. `ExploreRead.standingCut` is optional, and a prefix without it stops with `authority-unavailable`.\n- **Recorded aliases.** `explore` takes an alias only when the actor, key, scope, meaning, fact and revisions equal the replica's own checked entry. Otherwise it stops `source`.\n- No credential, header or custody path changes beyond these checks.\n\n## Simplification\n`scope-client.ts` grows by about 435 lines. Three paths (`retainAuthorizations`, `#retainComposition`, `submit`) each catch `PendingVia` and re-plan. They share `#prepareVia`, `#checkViaPrerequisites` and `#checkViaOrder`, so the logic is not copied, but control flow by exception across three callers is the next thing to fold. I do not ask for it here.\n\n## Non-blocking\n1. **Public list type.** Name `AuthorizationRequestView` in `packages/client/README.md` when a later head documents the requests list. No document mentions the list today.\n2. **Sync cost.** `#publicationCut` now reads all retained authorization records on every sync. The store bounds retention (64 unsigned positions), so the cost is small. Re-measure if a client keeps many waiting requests.\n3. **Exception control flow.** See Simplification.\n4. **Design note.** The status paragraph in `notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md` now has one line longer than the paragraph's wrap. Rewrap it at the next edit.\n\n## Deployment\nThe changed paths are client source and tests plus two notes. No Worker source, schema, table or generated asset changes, so rollback is safe. Read the DO rate after any deployment that bundles the client (`scripts/do-rate.mjs`).","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:33a4b7ad668817ccf42f9723fe80cc95e1eb7044","binding":"assigned","head":"4f801add015f09c1428839ae244b643516762f9c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ede40e961729cdc99f0ef72f6fe0604b894152ed\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:adf6f94b490e85529ac1dccc00e093fd2a8fff9e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:815feca558a421ac93d2c910e453529a703520ce","review_